# A drive without a diskette, a fixed disk without a partition (roadmap
# os-server.md P9): errors, never a hang. By DOS's letters, since a volume
# not there has no name in /mnt (disk-scheduler.md M8, D20): B's no
# diskette, ENXIO; D's no FAT12, EIO.
program: sh
media: B ejected
media: D blank
# DOSBox-X takes no diskette out and blanks no disk (media:).
emulators: bochs mame
keys: ls b:; ls d:; echo x > b:/x.txt\n
---
rx286, test build
/mnt/rx286$ ls b:; ls d:; echo x > b:/x.txt
b:: no such device
d:: input/output error
sh: b:/x.txt: no such device
/mnt/rx286$
